  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "new architecture support",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "MiMoForCausalLM was absent from architecture dispatch; the change adds a Llama-derived implementation explicitly excluding MTP layers.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_09335d5eea16423b80edb6760e07e6df",
          "call_479dc166d40c4b25a10b306b834c5d09",
          "call_9fff3f3caefd4fc98c6e0f96de46e5ce"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Registration and the derived-model mapping work together: Config.from_directory selects MiMoConfig, which supplies {'text': MiMoModel}; Model.from_config then constructs that subclass rather than the default LlamaModel.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_815b6891af054b6e85c26dbae8b88d22",
          "call_7efa4087e3ad4748940d32c2273a43d2",
          "call_9fff3f3caefd4fc98c6e0f96de46e5ce"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "MiMo gains the existing Llama configuration and decoder construction without a new execution implementation. This establishes dispatch support, not measured checkpoint equivalence or MTP support.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_9fff3f3caefd4fc98c6e0f96de46e5ce",
          "call_41b01627d27b4225b77079349473e536"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "The initial models ancestor entry was read. It documents shared Llama construction, checkpoint naming and missing sliding-window propagation in related wrappers.",
        "basis": "ancestor",
        "evidence": [
          "call_b129e7c865634ddaa557f231146f11f8"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "PR #4, 'chore: update config.py', concerns a spelling correction. Issue #7, 'quantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate', reports an extension/toolchain problem. Issue #33, 'Error converting model', reports file-opening failures and later GLM4 sampling trouble. Their overlap with inspected configuration or compilation files is contextual; no causal connection to the MiMo change is established.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_325936f1dea74e83bc0f92cd774bb955",
          "call_1e79e0e179ca4d148ead06eb7129ff7e",
          "call_712b07f896244c8dab50d2b2991c12e0",
          "call_674d068510974a4faf7f9896250cdef8"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model loading, conversion, generation or GPU tests were executed. The Python check used transcribed integer metadata only.",
      "Checkpoint tensor headers and reference modeling implementations were not inspected; configuration agreement alone does not establish weight-name coverage, bias handling or numerical equivalence.",
      "MTP is intentionally excluded. Compatibility beyond the five inspected configurations remains unestablished."
    ],
    "links": [
      "543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "MiMo dispatch through the Llama decoder",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "MiMo follows the existing Mistral and Qwen2 wrapper pattern: an architecture-specific config supplies its text model class, and the model delegates construction to LlamaModel. Those existing wrappers apply no additional constructor guards that the new wrapper omits.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_17da75d1c0854ac9b9d1dfdf426526d2",
              "call_6ca4223f99d440a992698a61d932b330",
              "call_07d706bbcf314f5facda339c7ecdafbe",
              "call_9fff3f3caefd4fc98c6e0f96de46e5ce"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Inherited construction creates model.embed_tokens, num_hidden_layers transformer blocks, model.norm and lm_head. Blocks use input/post-attention RMSNorm, separate q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj attention projections and gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj MLP projections. The config accepts SiLU, defaults missing KV-head count to query-head count, and derives missing head width from hidden_size divided by query-head count.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_41b01627d27b4225b77079349473e536"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "All five inspected XiaomiMiMo configs match the new architecture identifier and inherited core dimensions: MiMo-7B-Base, MiMo-7B-RL, MiMo-7B-RL-0530, MiMo-7B-RL-Zero and MiMo-7B-SFT each specify 36 layers, hidden width 4096, intermediate width 11008, 32 query heads, eight KV heads and explicit head width 128. Each supplies SiLU, RMS epsilon 1e-5 and untied embeddings, so the corresponding inherited defaults are not needed.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5b720285f489452d9735101546d9b7f4",
              "call_532adc31c1174ace89314a55bbfd3e8e",
              "call_db0668b929d04004b62b2d815d328073",
              "call_a3e97aa525d34a14adb3424f55792c30",
              "call_6aa32bb89b664c7d96b6339b120652f6",
              "call_41b01627d27b4225b77079349473e536"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The inherited RoPE reader consumes theta 640000 for each model. Base, RL, RL-Zero and SFT declare 32768 maximum positions; RL-0530 declares 65536 and null rope_scaling. All five disable sliding-window attention. The unchanged Llama constructor still does not propagate sliding-window settings, but these configurations do not request that behavior.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_815b6891af054b6e85c26dbae8b88d22",
              "call_41b01627d27b4225b77079349473e536",
              "call_5b720285f489452d9735101546d9b7f4",
              "call_532adc31c1174ace89314a55bbfd3e8e",
              "call_db0668b929d04004b62b2d815d328073",
              "call_a3e97aa525d34a14adb3424f55792c30",
              "call_6aa32bb89b664c7d96b6339b120652f6"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Each inspected configuration declares one next-token-prediction layer, but MiMo adds no constructor logic for it: the inherited loop builds only decoder indices 0 through 35. This is the concrete boundary of the change's 'no MTP yet' scope.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_9fff3f3caefd4fc98c6e0f96de46e5ce",
              "call_41b01627d27b4225b77079349473e536",
              "call_5b720285f489452d9735101546d9b7f4",
              "call_532adc31c1174ace89314a55bbfd3e8e",
              "call_db0668b929d04004b62b2d815d328073",
              "call_a3e97aa525d34a14adb3424f55792c30",
              "call_6aa32bb89b664c7d96b6339b120652f6"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library arithmetic check gives query width 4096, KV width 1024, four query heads per KV head and 39 top-level modules. It checks the transcribed dimensions and construction count, not repository execution.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_ccabf65822944a69a0a76be70d82f7bd"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Registers MiMoForCausalLM through thin Llama-derived classes, enabling ordinary decoder construction while deliberately leaving MTP unsupported."
  },
